cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Chain of Title: launch provenance for Solana"
message: >-
  If you use this archive or the code that produces it, please cite it. If you
  cite a specific finding, cite the dated release you read rather than the
  repository, because the record grows daily and coverage is part of the data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bomhoff
    given-names: Michael
    email: hello@chainoftitle.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/mike-totum/chain-of-title"
url: "https://chainoftitle.org"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  A public archive of launch-time provenance for Solana tokens. For every launch
  it records what the token was at birth: the share of supply the creator took in
  the creation transaction, every distinct outside wallet that bought on the
  bonding curve, how long the curve took to fill, whether a single buy completed
  it, and whether the creator sold. These facts are observable only while a launch
  happens and cannot be recovered by present-tense inspection once the float has
  been spread across wallets, which is why they are recorded live rather than
  inferred later. Coverage is published alongside the data: a launch that happened
  while the collector was down is reported as unobserved rather than as anything
  else. The record is released into the public domain under CC0; the code that
  produces it is AGPL-3.0-or-later.
keywords:
  - Solana
  - provenance
  - token security
  - open data
  - public goods
  - blockchain
